  "screen.terrafabrica.guide": "Terra Fabrica Guide",
  "gui.terrafabrica.guide.page": "Page %s / %s",
  "gui.terrafabrica.guide.research": "Research",
  "gui.terrafabrica.guide.close": "Close",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.title": "About",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.line.1": "A science and technology progression: from a rock chunk to a power plant. Era I is steam and mechanics, Era II is steel, electricity and chemistry.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.line.2": "Every value is SI: energy in joules (J), power in watts (W), temperature in kelvin (K), pressure in pascals (Pa), voltage in volts (V), current in amperes (A).",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.line.3": "Machine buffers store joules. 1 FE = 2.5 J; conversion rounds down, so energy never appears from nothing.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.line.4": "Rock replaces ore: it cannot be smelted directly — crush first, then enrich.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.line.5": "Progress is gated by research: while a tree node is locked a machine answers \"Research required\".",
  "guide.terrafabrica.intro.line.6": "The vanilla world stays intact: ores, recipes and worldgen remain, rock appears beside them.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.title": "Units and formulas",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.1": "Shaft power: P = (2π · RPM / 60) · M with torque in N·m. Every shaft has a torque limit.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.2": "20 ticks = 1 second; 1 kWh = 3.6 MJ. Process energy is power times seconds.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.3": "Heat: Q = C · ΔT. Each furnace has its own heat capacity and temperature ceiling.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.4": "Steam efficiency: Newcomen 0.5–1 %, Watt 5–8 %, turbines 15–25 %. The value is shown in the tooltip.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.5": "Electricity: the generator produces 50 Hz at 10 kV; transformers change voltage and the three cable classes lose different shares of power.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.6": "A steam turbine needs 1–3 MPa and 300–400 °C: lower pressure means lower output.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.units.line.7": "All numbers are visible in the machine GUI: temperature, RPM, torque, power, status.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.title": "Rock and enrichment",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.line.1": "Rock comes in poor, normal and rich variants — 30 % / 60 % / 10 % of veins, in stone and in deepslate.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.line.2": "A pickaxe yields 1, 2 or 3 chunks. Silk touch keeps the block intact, Fortune adds chunks.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.line.3": "Crusher: 1 chunk to 1 powder, 50 kJ and 5 seconds.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.line.4": "Separator: 2 powder to 1 concentrate for another 50 kJ. That is 0.9 concentrate per rock — a visible 10 % loss.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.line.5": "Concentrate smelts: copper and tin one to one, iron two concentrates per pig iron ingot.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.porodes.line.6": "Rich rock yields three times the chunks but is rare — worth hunting for.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.title": "Era I: steam and mechanics",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.1": "Furnaces: primitive (900 °C), bloomery (1300 °C), small blast furnace 3×3×5 (1500 °C), puddling 3×3×3, crucible 2×2×2.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.2": "Drives: water wheel 5–30 kW (60 % efficiency), windmill up to 20 kW (50 %), Newcomen engine 5–10 kW, Watt engine 20–100 kW.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.3": "Transmission: shaft, gear, belt, pulley, gearbox with 1:1, 2:1, 1:2, 1:4, 1:8 ratios; a belt loses 10–20 %.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.4": "Machine tools are deliberately single-block: lathe, drill press, milling, grinding, power hammer. Multiblocks would only slow the era down.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.5": "Chemistry: pyrite roasting gives SO₂, the lead chamber gives 78 % sulfuric acid, Solvay gives soda, the glass furnace gives glass.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.6": "Transport: rails, minecarts with three stacks, conveyor at 1 m/s, small steam locomotive 2×3×2.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era1.line.7": "The era ends with the \"Transition to Era II\" node, which unlocks coking and steel.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.title": "Era II: steel, power, chemistry",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.1": "The coke oven yields coke, coal tar and lighting gas — by-products are never wasted.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.2": "Metallurgy: coke blast furnace 5×5×10, Bessemer converter, open hearth, arc furnace at 100 kW and 2000 °C.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.3": "Rolling and drawing: plates, rods and three wire classes for different voltages.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.4": "Alloys with strict compositions: Fe-18Cr-8Ni, Ni-25Cr-20Co-1.5Nb-1.5Ti-0.5Al, Ti-6Al-4V.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.5": "Power: steam turbine 3×3×5, gas turbine, combined cycle, generator 3×3×3 (50 Hz, 10 kV), transformer, electric motor, lead-acid battery.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.6": "Chemistry: air separation, water electrolysis, ammonia (400–500 °C, 20–30 MPa, iron catalyst poisoned by sulfur), Ostwald, contact acid, halite electrolysis.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.7": "Aluminium: electrolysis at 960 °C in cryolite, 13–15 MWh per tonne, fluorine capture is mandatory.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.era2.line.8": "Communication and automation: telegraph, telephone, radio, tube computer, and the sensor → controller → actuator chain. The last node is \"Transition to Era III\".",
  "guide.terrafabrica.research.title": "Research",
  "guide.terrafabrica.research.line.1": "Left-click a yellow node to start research when prerequisites are met and resources are at hand.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.research.line.2": "While a node is locked the machine refuses the recipe and reports the cost — it is simply gated.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.research.line.3": "Progress ticks on the server: time and costs are in the node tooltip, the client only renders it.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.research.line.4": "Era III is intentionally not implemented in this version — the tree ends at its transition node.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.datapack.title": "Datapack and compatibility",
  "guide.terrafabrica.datapack.line.1": "Every process is a datapack recipe: data/terrafabrica/recipe/<machine>/<name>.json.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.datapack.line.2": "Recipe fields: ingredients, counts, results, energy (J), ticks, research, fluid_in, fluid_out, min_temperature, min_pressure.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.datapack.line.3": "The counts field sets exact amounts: that is how the separator requires two powder per concentrate.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.datapack.line.4": "Tags: terrafabrica:porodes, ingots/<metal>, plates, wires, tools, plus minecraft:mineable/pickaxe and needs_*_tool.",
  "guide.terrafabrica.datapack.line.5": "The tools/validate_data.py and tools/audit_resources.py scripts plus the tests catch mismatches before the game starts.",
